# Real variable files: they name your account's region, domain and hosted zone, and they are
# per-operator. The .example is the committed one.
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example

# State must never be committed. It contains the generated database password and Redis token in
# plain text — which is also why the backend bucket in README.md is encrypted and access-
# controlled rather than "just a bucket".
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
crash.log

# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored. It pins each provider to a specific version
# and records its hashes, which is the same supply-chain control as a committed pnpm-lock.yaml or
# uv.lock — without it, two people init the same configuration and get different providers.

# Overriding the root .gitignore, which excludes this file globally. It belongs in version
# control: it pins each provider to an exact version and records its hashes, the same
# supply-chain control as pnpm-lock.yaml or uv.lock.
!.terraform.lock.hcl
